# Model Routing (opencode-go landscape, ratified 2026-08-01, re-routed 2026-08-02, re-paired 2026-08-20, Ox Alpha temp 2026-08-21)

## Canonical relationship

This file is the always-injected routing policy. The live implementation lives in
`~/.omo/omo.jsonc` (agents map, categories map,
background_task.modelConcurrency). `opencode.jsonc` base model/small_model/agents are
untouched by routing. **Where this file and the config differ, the config wins** (it
executes); this file records intent so future edits stay justified.

## Routing table (agent → model → fallback)

| Agent | Model | Fallback |
|---|---|---|
| oracle / prometheus / metis / momus / ultrabrain | `opencode/x-preview-f-free` | `opencode-go/glm-5.2` |
| test-writer / review | `opencode-go/gpt-5.6-luna` | (existing) |
| architect / sisyphus / build / worker | `opencode/x-preview-f-free` | `opencode-go/mimo-v2.5` |
| hephaestus / atlas | `opencode-go/deepseek-v4-flash` | (existing; both disabled) |
| explore / scout / quick / librarian / multimodal-looker / sisyphus-junior / writing / git | `opencode/x-preview-f-free` | (existing) |
| general | category `unspecified-low` | (existing) |

## Category table

| Category | Model |
|---|---|
| ultrabrain | `opencode/x-preview-f-free` |
| unspecified-high / artistry / deep | `opencode/x-preview-f-free` |
| visual-engineering | `opencode-go/minimax-m3` |
| writing / git / quick / unspecified-low | `opencode/x-preview-f-free` |

- **Ox Alpha as temporary free workhorse (routed 2026-08-21)**: stealth/reasoning model
  (`opencode/x-preview-f-free`), announced Aug 20 2026, FREE for ~1 week on Zen
  ($0.00/$0.00 — no dollar quota during the window). 1M ctx, tool calling, reasoning-capable
  (live-verified Aug 21 via API: returns `reasoning_content`). ZERO-RETENTION — does NOT
  train on user data (unlike Big Pickle / MiMo-free / Hy3-free / Nemotron-free / Muse
  Contributor-free). Community consensus: likely Zhipu GLM's stealth model (→ plausibly
  GLM-5.2/5.3 class, Akita 92-94/A.1) — UNCONFIRMED. Quality UNVERIFIED at launch (no
  SWE-bench/Akita/BenchLM row; LMMarketCap 20/100 is a crude composite) — a deliberate
  bet, hedged by fallback chains preserving the previous best as fallback[1].
  - **Budget rationale (Aug 17 2026 DeepSeek price increase)**: V4 Flash API prices roughly
  doubled; OpenCode cut its Go-plan quota to 7,600 req/5h (from ~63,300) and monthly pool
  to $30 (from $60). Flash is no longer the cheap volume workhorse — worst of both worlds.
  User's $10/mo Go plan + free Zen tier forces a **pareto line on the cheap side**: while
  Ox Alpha is free it beats every paid option on cost AND (probably) quality, so it
  temporarily replaces BOTH the volume tier (MiMo-V2.5) and the quality tier (GLM-5.2).
  - **MiMo-V2.5 → fallback/second (was volume workhorse 2026-08-20)**: 30,100 req/5h — the
  only true 30k+ paid model that does NOT train on user data (Muse Spark 1.2 Contributor
  is 45,300/5h but trains on data; Hy3's 8x promo expired → 4,300/5h, off the volume
  table). Cheapest per-request paid model; independently verified WEAKER than Flash
  (Akita 67/B vs 78/B, failed all 4 Tier-A criteria) — the OMO harness compensates. Now
  sits as fallback[1] on the volume agents.
  - **GLM-5.2 → fallback/second (was hard-reasoning 2026-08-20)**: Akita 92/A.1 (independently
  verified), BenchLM coding 88th pct, strong agentic — best quality-per-quota at
  880 req/5h, $60/mo. Now sits as fallback[1] on the reasoning/planning agents (oracle,
  prometheus, metis, momus, ultrabrain). (Replaces the old 'No GLM-5.2 on this platform'
  rule — superseded when Flash lost its edge.)
- **Muse Spark 1.2 Contributor — SINGAPORE-VERIFIED (2026-08-21)**: live API test from SG
  returned HTTP 200 (no region block). $0.10/$0.20, 45,300 req/5h — cheapest paid AND
  biggest Go-plan quota. Caveat: TRAINS on user data (that's the discount). Held as the
  post-Ox-Alpha default candidate. On Zen free tier it also trains on data.
  - **fallback_models allowlist (2026-08-02/03, claude-opus-5 incident)**: every agent/category
  carries a 5-entry allowlist suppressing OMO's HARDCODED AGENT_MODEL_REQUIREMENTS chain
  (sisyphus chain[0] was claude-opus-5/anthropic — fired on transient errors despite
  disabled_providers; see docs/INCIDENTS.md). Pattern now: `fallback_models[0]` = primary
  model, `[1]` = previous best (glm-5.2 or mimo-v2.5), tail `[2..4]` = gpt-5.6-luna,
  minimax-m3, deepseek-v4-flash-free. When Ox Alpha's free window ends, fallback
  auto-catches if it 404s; if it becomes paid, re-benchmark before keeping it.
  - **GPT 5.6 Luna on code-gen**: budget frontier (SWE-Pro 62.7, coding rank #6,
  $0.20/$1.20 — 1/12 of Max's input price, 2,050 req/5h). **Luna is served via OpenAI
  `/responses`, not chat/completions** — works only through opencode's BUILT-IN
  opencode-go provider, which auto-selects transport per model. Also the top-level
  `opencode.jsonc` default model (set 2026-08-20). review/test-writer stay here.
  - **MiniMax M3 only on visual-engineering**: the one slot that genuinely needs image/video
  input. Agentic numbers are vendor-only and BenchLM-independent ranks it weak (#96/128
  agentic, 40.5/100); flash 0731 dominates (TB2.1 82.7 vs 66.0) at 2.7× less. M3
  supersedes minimax-m2.7.
  - **DeepSeek V4 Flash effectively retired from primary routing**: `opencode-go/deepseek-v4-flash`
  appears ONLY on the two DISABLED agents (atlas, hephaestus) and as a mid-chain fallback
  tail on a few agents. Free-tier `deepseek-v4-flash-free` / `mimo-v2.5-free` remain as
  fallback tail — no primary routing (Ox Alpha covers those slots).
  - **qwen3.7-plus over qwen3.6-plus**: 3.6-plus is superseded and has a known tool-call-loop
  bug. (qwen3.6-plus + minimax-m2.7 removed from modelConcurrency; qwen3.7-max concurrency 0.)

## NOT-list (do not do)

1. **NEVER add a custom `opencode-go` provider entry with
   `@ai-sdk/openai-compatible`** — it breaks gpt-5.6-luna (responses-only
   transport). The built-in opencode-go provider handles per-model transport.
2. No Kimi K3 ($3/$15), no Grok 4.5 ($2/$6) — spend stays below that tier.
3. No Qwen3.7 Max ($2.50/$7.50) — hallucination-prone (Akita v2 51/C); concurrency 0.
4. No Muse Spark 1.2 Contributor as PRIMARY unless you accept data-training — it
   trains on prompts/completions (the discount). Reserve for the post-Ox-Alpha fallback.
5. Routing scope only — no permission/hook/agent-definition/provider changes.
6. No non-opencode-go / non-deepseek providers.
7. No `opencode-go/deepseek-v4-pro` — still the Apr preview; not worth the spend.
8. **Ox Alpha is a temporary free bet** — do not bake permanent reliance on it; the
   fallback chain is the exit. When the free window ends, re-benchmark before keeping it.
9. **Hy3: SKIP** (input $0.14 = MiMo but output $0.58 2×, quota 4,300/5h) — no edge.

## Budget layering

Three enforcement layers (deliberate, not a conflict): soft routing target ~$15/mo
(falsification trigger above) → hard block via routing + `modelConcurrency` caps
(per-model concurrency zeros out budget-blocked models; qwen3.7-max concurrency=0 since 2026-08-02)
→ monitoring ceiling $60/mo. Dead budget files `cost-guard.config.json` + `token-monitor.json` deleted 2026-08-02 (commit a8cb111).

## Refresh trigger

Lightweight periodic re-review (LANDSCAPE-lite): when the user senses the
landscape shifted, or a model is added/retired on opencode.ai/docs/go, or
falsification signals appear (frontier outputs no measurable gain ~2 weeks, main
agent 429-starvation, spend >$15/mo). Re-verify against the live model list
(https://opencode.ai/zen/go/v1/models) and models.dev before changing anything.

## Benchmark integrity (2026-08-03)

When comparing models during LANDSCAPE checks, cite ONLY contamination-resistant
benches. **SWE-bench Verified is DEAD as a signal** — OpenAI Frontier Evals
stopped reporting it (Apr 2026): audit found >60% of tasks unsolvable-as-written,
models reproduce gold patches VERBATIM from task ID, saturated at 93.9%;
any score >80% warrants harness/tool-access scrutiny. Do NOT cite it.

Trustworthy: SWE-bench Pro (contamination-resistant by design — GPL-copyleft
+ private repos, held-out/commercial subsets; frontier ~59% on Pro vs 80-95%
on Verified), LiveCodeBench (time-split, contamination-free by design), HLE +
PaperBench (novel/fail-safe design). Caveat-only: Terminal-Bench 2.1 (canary
"largely symbolic safeguard" per its own paper; interactive-CLI harder to game
but vendor-reported numbers like flash 0731's 82.7 need independent confirm),
BenchLM (aggregate), NL2Repo/Cybergym/Toolathlon/DSBench/DeepSWE (vendor-reported).
